state/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
# Build output from `pip install .` / `python -m build`. Regenerable, and it duplicates
# every engine source file — committing it once put 7,500 lines of copies into history.
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# PERSONAL ABILITY SETS. `workspace/<name>/` is where someone's own abilities live — their own git
# repository, nested inside this checkout on purpose: the trust boundary is an ENGINE_TREE prefix
# check, so an ability set here is implicitly trusted (their own code) while one outside the tree
# must be approved file by file. Measured: moving the same nine abilities to a sibling directory
# made 9 of 12 fail load with "code from outside this engine's own tree".
#
# Ignored, never tracked: this repository ships the engine and its samples. A guard in tests/
# asserts nothing under here is tracked, because the failure is one accidental `git add -A`.
# workspace/

# Run output inside the shipped sample directory. The folders are tracked (a sample whose declared
# capability reports absent on a fresh clone is a bad first sentence); what a run writes into them is
# not — it is state, and it would show up as a dirty tree after every walk of the sample flow.
abilities/sample-lib/sample/*/*.json
